course: dictionary
lesson: 11993
title: Sea songs and the word chanty
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A chanty is a song that sailors sang long ago while they worked together. Read the clues around the word. «The sailors sang a chanty as they pulled the heavy ropes.» Pulling ropes is hard work, and singing helps a crew work together, so a chanty must be a work song.
explain: «One sailor sang the first line, and the whole crew answered.» Sailors answering a singer tells you the song had a call and a reply. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A song that workers sang together fits, so chanty means a sea song.
explain: Be careful: «The fisherman's shanty stood on the beach.» Shanty is spelled the same as chanty in some books, but here it is a rough hut, not a song. Chanty can also be spelled chantey. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A chanty is a song that sailors sang long ago while they worked.
fact: Chanty can also be spelled shanty or chantey when it means a sea song.
fact: Sailors sang chanties to keep a strong beat, so everyone could pull at the same moment.
fact: One person sang a line, and the crew answered.
fact: A shanty can also mean a rough hut. That is a different meaning, so check the sentence.
exercise: «The sailors sang a chanty as they pulled the ropes.» What is a chanty? | A rough hut by the sea | *A song sailors sang while they worked together | A ship's cook | A kind of rope
exercise: «The crew sang the chanty loudly as they hauled the net.» Find and copy one word that tells you the crew was working. | crew | sang | loudly | *hauled
exercise: Nadia says chanty means a rough hut, like a shanty. What is the real meaning of chanty? | A small sailing boat | A rough hut on a beach | A loud shout from a sailor | *A song sailors sang while working together
test: «The sea chanty had a strong beat that helped everyone pull together.» What was the sea chanty used for? | To sink old boats | To cook supper for the crew | *To help sailors pull at the same moment | To put out fires
test: «The old shanty by the harbour had a leaking roof.» In this sentence, what does shanty mean? | A kind of fish | A harbour ship | A sea song | *A rough hut
exam: Jayden reads «The sailors sang as they hauled the anchor.» What is the best clue that the song was a work song? | They were sleeping under the stars | *They were hauling the anchor together | They were reading books | They were sitting by a warm fire
